{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GVY", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{decent-spaces-section-specializations}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7bb433b62527c9532b7cda58d18df1d287d4fa54dc7293b3e67e0f1d20f7e0a8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the analogue of\nDecent Spaces, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:87bcc4ef1451686adb0a991f62460ff8d9be576fe45580a2e8c3c7bd66140d6a", "unit_id": "tag:0GVY:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GVY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$x' \\leadsto x$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0006": "$u \\in |U|$", "MATH_0007": "$f(u) = x$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\mathcal{X}, x')$", "MATH_0009": "$u' \\leadsto u$", "MATH_0010": "$|U|$", "MATH_0011": "$f(u') = x'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-UR-quasi-compact-above-x}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-specialization}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:25891ef011bdc2224e394695d4cdfbac93752a62945abc958a884d518238799b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5934835495cec24341b14b7dc117abb427053b80e615d43d06002abbc4a77bbd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a smooth morphism where <MATH_0003> is an algebraic space. Let\n<MATH_0004> be a specialization of points of <MATH_0005>.\nLet <MATH_0006> with <MATH_0007>. If <MATH_0008> satisfy the\nequivalent conditions of Properties of Stacks,\nLemma <REF_0001>,\nthen there exists a specialization\n<MATH_0009> in <MATH_0010> with <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:35847270b5125b913062f17a32d9b3e272e8e64b8c16b4a8b34afe29ef9be1c5", "unit_id": "tag:0GVZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GVY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$(U_1, u_1) \\to (U, u)$", "MATH_0002": "$U_1$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U_1$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$R = U \\times_\\mathcal{X} U$", "MATH_0007": "$t, s : R \\to U$", "MATH_0008": "$w \\in U$", "MATH_0009": "$x'$", "MATH_0010": "$f : |U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0011": "$x'$", "MATH_0012": "$F' = t^{-1}(w) = R \\times_{t, U} w$", "MATH_0013": "$t : R \\to U$", "MATH_0014": "$w$", "MATH_0015": "$T$", "MATH_0016": "$T \\to F'$", "MATH_0017": "$x' \\leadsto x$", "MATH_0018": "$u$", "MATH_0019": "$$\nT \\to F' \\to R \\xrightarrow{s} U\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$|U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}'|$", "MATH_0021": "$x'$", "MATH_0022": "$u \\in V \\subset |U|$", "MATH_0023": "$f(V)$", "MATH_0024": "$x$", "MATH_0025": "$x'$", "MATH_0026": "$u' \\in |U|$", "MATH_0027": "$|U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0028": "$x'$", "MATH_0029": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-reach-points-scheme-theoretic-image}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:23dbdbc490436ff546daeced8877534e26356f640ef2210c9198e868453d7a5f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:44e56e2985b0bb1002045302db78e78975a88021cb1f92fbc6f0ee8b3154c80c", "source_text": "Choose an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0001> where <MATH_0002>\nis an affine scheme. Then we may and do replace <MATH_0003> by <MATH_0004>.\nThus we may assume <MATH_0005> is an affine scheme.\nConsider the algebraic space <MATH_0006>\nwith smooth projections <MATH_0007>.\nChoose a point <MATH_0008> mapping to <MATH_0009>; this is possible as\n<MATH_0010> is open.\nBy our assumption on <MATH_0011> the fibre\n<MATH_0012>\nof <MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014> is a quasi-compact algebraic space.\nChoose an affine scheme <MATH_0015> and a surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\n<MATH_0016>. The fact that <MATH_0017> means that <MATH_0018> is in\nthe closure of the image of the morphism\n<MATH_0019>\nNamely, this image is the fibre of <MATH_0020>\nover <MATH_0021>; if some <MATH_0022> open is disjoint\nfrom this fibre, then <MATH_0023> is an open neighbourhood of <MATH_0024>\nnot containing <MATH_0025>; contradiction.\nThus by Morphisms, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nwe see that  there exists <MATH_0026> in the fibre\nof <MATH_0027> over <MATH_0028> which specializes to <MATH_0029>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa803641a544f7d83b8d2e98cc780abc0e9676beab222d6de91d5ccc29ad4180", "unit_id": "tag:0GVZ:proof"}
